          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does one ENSŌ bowl last?",
            "answer": "<p>45–60 min with the standard cup; up to 120 min with a Flower Cup (stir halfway).</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_UTGXdV": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I mix two flavours in one bowl?",
            "answer": "<p>Absolutely. Layer or split 50/50—just keep total mass under 15g and leave the airway clear. Put mint or spice notes on top for best effect.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_GtcLPa": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What are the ENSŌ disposable cups for?",
            "answer": "<p>Ten single-use aluminium cups ship with each kit—ideal for sticky mixes or rapid swaps. Rinse gently for up to three uses, then recycle.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_Xtnxpk": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I load more than 15 g in ENSŌ?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes—add the Flower Cup or Glass Collar accessory to fit up to 20g.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_LXBNjR": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use dark leaf tobacco in ENSŌ?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, ENSŌ is designed for every tobacco and herbal molasses. For dark leafs we recommend to give it more heating time after pre-heat and use smaller leafs.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_VWMMe4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which tobaccos or herbal blends work best with ENSŌ?",
            "answer": "<p>ENSŌ handles any moist, molasses-based shisha—dark-leaf or blonde—as well as herbal mixes. Smaller leafs and semi-dense packing works the best. If your chosen tobacco have large leafs, you can cut them with scissors before loading into the bowl.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_b9chQP": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much should I load and how should I pack it ENSŌ?",
            "answer": "<p>Place 8 – 15g in the ceramic cup, semi-dense with a central airway. Start at 175 °C for 5–8 min, then step up 30–45 ° as needed.<br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/4FlQ9ACwn00?si=58nw5sS5eecGmuC1\" target=\"_blank\">(Watch ▶ Mastering ENSŌ)</a></p>"
          }
        }
